.nh
.TH "TEAMS" "1" "Oct 2026" "teams dev" "teams Manual"

.SH NAME
teams-auth-status - Show the signed-in account, its scopes and the token store


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBteams auth status [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show who you are signed in as, which scopes the current token carries (the
\fBscp\fR claim lists every consented scope), and where the token cache lives.

.PP
Exits 3 when the profile is not signed in or the refresh token is dead.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--admin-request\fP[=false]
	print the admin-consent and redirect-URI changes to request

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for status


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also honours NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	never prompt; fail fast instead

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (default: the configured default_profile)

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress progress messages on stderr

.PP
\fB--read-only\fP[=false]
	refuse write commands

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	verbose diagnostics on stderr (-v, -vv)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBteams-auth(1)\fP
